e, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6063918a-22c9-40c6-8831-cbf3519aa926","uuid":"86625bcb-808a-4232-b17b-68fcdefa37da","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json","content":"{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n  },\n  \"structure\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n      \"title\": null,\n      \"index\": 1,\n      \"start_position\": 28,\n      \"end_position\": 13811,\n      \"word_count\": 2443,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\",\n        \"Courtiers\",\n        \"Musicians\",\n        \"Buffoons\",\n        \"Improvisatori\",\n        \"Ballet-dancers\",\n        \"Beauty\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the 'Red Death,' a horrific plague marked by sharp pains, profuse bleeding, and scarlet stains that isolate victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, fortified abbey, where he provides endless entertainment and barricades all exits to ensure safety. Months later, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each lit by blood-red firelight through stained-glass windows, culminating in a black chamber with scarlet panes and a massive ebony clock that halts all activity with its hourly chime. When a mysterious figure dressed as the Red Death appears—dripping in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask—the courtiers are paralyzed by terror, and the prince, enraged, pursues the intruder through all seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse dead upon confronting the figure, who is revealed to be the plague itself; one by one, all revelers die as the clock stops and darkness claims the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"Prospero\",\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a self-indulgent and tyrannical ruler who isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the plague, prioritizing his own safety and pleasure over the lives of others. His actions—sealing the abbey, hosting a lavish ball during a deadly epidemic, and violently pursuing a masked figure—reveal a man consumed by arrogance, fear, and a desire to assert control, ultimately leading to his death when he confronts the embodiment of the plague he sought to evade.\",\n          \"source_position\": 1894,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero isolates himself and a thousand courtiers in a fortified abbey to escape the plague\",\n          \"quote\": \"Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, fortified abbey, where he provides endless entertainment and barricades all exits to ensure safety.\",\n          \"position\": \"Chapter 1\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He hosts a lavish masked ball during the height of the plague\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was toward the close of the fifth or sixth month of his seclusion, and while the pestilence raged most furiously abroad, that the Prince Prospero entertained his thousand friends at a masked ball of the most unusual magnificence.\",\n          \"position\": \"Context 1\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He reacts with rage and violence when confronted by a masked figure resembling the plague\",\n          \"quote\": \"insult us with this blasphemous mockery? Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": \"Context 3\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He pursues the masked figure with a dagger, driven by rage and fear\",\n          \"quote\": \"It was then, however, that the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers, while none followed him on account of a deadly terror that had...\",\n          \"position\": \"Context 5\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He dies upon confronting the masked figure, who is revealed to be the plague incarnate\",\n          \"quote\": \"There was a sharp cry -- and the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero.\",\n          \"position\": \"Context 6\",\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 7,\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pronunciations\": [\n    {\n      \"word\": \"Prospero\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"proper_noun\",\n      \"occurrences\": 18,\n      \"first_