raph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 5609,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...s and folly, and made whispering vows, each to the other, that the next chiming of the clock should produce in them no similar emotion; and then, after the lapse of sixty minutes, (which embrace three thousa...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: vegetables (PROH-doos); to make (pruh-DOOS)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 11611,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"glossary\": null,\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"structure\": {\n      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n      \"has_titles\": false,\n      \"has_parts\": false,\n      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n    },\n    \"plot_summary\": {\n      \"plot_summary\": \"The story begins in the grip of a merciless plague known as the Red Death, which sweeps across the land with terrifying efficiency—causing agonizing pain, violent bleeding, and the telltale scarlet stains that mark its victims. Amid the chaos and despair, Prince Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and unyielding pride, chooses to defy fate by retreating with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, heavily fortified abbey. There, he constructs a world of opulence and illusion, sealing off all exits to shield them from the outside horror. For months, the revelers live in a state of suspended reality, indulging in music, dance, and lavish entertainment, unaware that their sanctuary is merely a temporary reprieve from inevitable doom.\\n\\nThe tension builds as Prospero hosts a grand masked ball in seven intricately decorated chambers, each illuminated by a different hue, culminating in a final, ominous black chamber lit by scarlet panes. The room houses a massive ebony clock that chimes each hour, halting all revelry and plunging the guests into silence and dread. The atmosphere grows increasingly oppressive, as the clock’s chimes serve as a grim reminder of time’s inexorable march. When a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, with blood-streaked garments and a mask resembling a corpse—the courtiers are paralyzed with fear. Prince Prospero, enraged by the intrusion and the violation of his sanctuary, draws a dagger and pursues the figure through the seven rooms, driven by a mix of fury and denial.\\n\\nThe climax unfolds in the black chamber, where the prince confronts the figure, only to collapse dead upon realizing the truth: the intruder is not a guest, but the plague personified. The revelation shatters the illusion of safety, and as the clock’s final chime echoes through the abbey, the revelers begin to fall one by one, succumbing to the very disease they had tried to escape. Darkness consumes the abbey, and the story ends with the complete annihilation of all who sought refuge in luxury and denial. The narrative underscores the futility of attempting to outrun fate, even through wealth, power, or isolation.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"timing\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 16.16,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"16.2s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 296.22,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"4m 56s\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 25.51,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"25.5s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 29.48,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"29.5s\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 73.73,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"1m 14s\"\n      },\n      \"total\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 446.33,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"7m 26s\"\n      },\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-01-19 02:44:41\",\n      \"ended_at\": \"2026-01-19 02:52:07\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"low_confidence_items\": [],\n  \"_analysis_metadata\": {\n    \"analyzed_at\": \"2026-01-19T02:52:17.532462\",\n    \"analyzer_version\": \"0.2.0\",\n    \"pipeline\": \"multi-agent\",\n    \"llm_model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n    \"llm_provider\": \"ollama\",\n    \"analysis_duration_seconds\": 456.3\n  },\n  \"_profiling\": {\n    \"stages\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Chapter Detection\",\n